EXT. SUNKEN GARDEN BENEATH A FALLEN STARSHIP - NIGHT

A hull the size of a cathedral lies crumpled across a valley. Under its arch, moss and glowing mushrooms have colonized a courtyard of broken tile.

Five figures circle a fire in the courtyard center.

IRENEUS BASKERVILLE-ADE (50s, wizard, coat of many pockets) feeds twigs to the flames.

MYRTLE "MYRT" OKONKWO-SPARROW (20s, bard, lute on her back) tunes a string.

HOLGER STAVROS-NWACHUKWU (30s, mercenary, scarred jaw) sharpens a long blade on a whetstone.

THEODORA "THEO" LAVENDER-OSEI (teens, apprentice, ink on her chin) copies glyphs from the hull onto a scroll.

And GRANDMAMA NKECHI WINTERBOURNE (80s, wrapped in quilts, eyes sharp as tacks) sits on a stool nearest the fire.

IRENEUS
(to the group)
We rest here till dawn.

HOLGER
Rest? With that thing over us?

IRENEUS
It's a ship, Holger. It's dead.

HOLGER
So were the last three things I fought.

MYRT
Holger, relax. Listen to this.

She plucks a gentle melody. The mushrooms pulse, brightening in time. Theo looks up from her scroll, startled.

THEO
Oh. They like it.

MYRT
Everything likes it.

HOLGER
(muttering)
Not me.

GRANDMAMA
You like it, boy. You just won't say.

HOLGER
Grandmama--

GRANDMAMA
Hush.

The fire cracks. Ireneus rises, brushing his coat.

IRENEUS
Theo, the glyphs. What do they say?

THEO
Um. "Do not wake the garden."

A long silence. The music stops. Myrt's hand freezes on the strings.

MYRT
Theo.

THEO
Sorry. I only just read it.

HOLGER
(rising, blade drawn)
Everyone quiet.

IRENEUS
Holger, put that away.

HOLGER
No.

Beneath them, the ground trembles. The mushrooms flare white, then red. A distant hum rises through the soil like a stirring giant.

MYRT
Ireneus.

IRENEUS
I know.

GRANDMAMA
(mildly, to the fire)
Well. That's the trouble with gardens.

The hull groans. Vines uncoil from the ceiling, thick as cables, and begin to descend. Holger swings at one. It splits, spills glowing sap, and lunges for his throat.

HOLGER
Theo, run!

THEO
Where?

HOLGER
Anywhere!

Myrt strikes a chord, wild, dissonant. The vines recoil. Ireneus hurls a handful of powder; it ignites in a flash of orange. Theo hauls Grandmama up by the elbow and they stumble toward the arch.

IRENEUS
(over the roar)
Don't look back!

MYRT
I am looking!

HOLGER
Then look faster!

A vine catches Holger's ankle. He topples. Myrt dives, slashes with her lute-strap. It parts. Together they scramble to their feet.

The five reach the arch just as the entire garden convulses, erupting into a roar of green light.

They tumble onto cold grass beyond. Behind them, the starship shudders, then lies still.

GRANDMAMA
(breathing hard)
Hm.

THEO
Grandmama?

GRANDMAMA
I'd like to go home now.
